    {
      "role": "agent",
      "text": "I'm starting the setup process to understand your company's needs. I've dispatched a command to gather initial information. I'll let you know what I find."
    },
    {
      "role": "user",
      "text": "Ok, go ahead."
    },
    {
      "role": "agent",
      "text": "I see that Jira Cloud is connected and working, and your GitHub connection needs to be reconnected. I can write new connections.\n\nTo start, could you tell me a bit about what your company builds and the technology stack you use?"
    },
    {
      "role": "user",
      "text": "We build logistics software, primarily using Java for backend services, React for frontends, and Python for data analysis and scripting. We use PostgreSQL databases."
    },
    {
      "role": "agent",
      "text": "Thanks for sharing that.\n\nNext, could you describe how your team reviews and ships changes? For example, do you use pull requests, a specific CI/CD pipeline, or other processes?"
    },
    {
      "role": "user",
      "text": "We use merge requests in GitLab for code reviews. Our CI/CD pipelines are also in GitLab, automating builds, tests, and deployments to our Kubernetes clusters."
    },
    {
      "role": "agent",
      "text": "Thanks for that information.\n\nNow, regarding your systems, which source control system do you use (e.g., GitHub, GitLab, Bitbucket), and is it cloud-hosted or self-managed?"
    },
    {
      "role": "user",
      "text": "We use self-managed GitLab. It's hosted internally at `gitlab.northwind.internal`."
    },
    {
      "role": "agent",
      "text": "Thank you.\n\nYou mentioned using PostgreSQL databases. Are these cloud-hosted or self-managed? Also, do you use any other significant systems like a specific issue tracker (besides Jira Cloud, which is already connected), package registries, or observability platforms?"
    },
    {
      "role": "user",
      "text": "Our PostgreSQL databases are self-managed. We use Jira Data Center for issue tracking, Artifactory for package management, and Prometheus and Grafana for observability."
    },
    {
      "role": "agent",
      "text": "Thanks for that.\n\nNext, could you tell me about your company's network? Do you use a proxy, TLS inspection, internal mirrors, or have any restrictions on inbound traffic?"
    },
    {
      "role": "user",
      "text": "Yes, we use a proxy for all external traffic and perform TLS inspection. We also have strict firewall rules restricting inbound connections. I don't think we use internal mirrors for external dependencies."
    },
    {
      "role": "agent",
      "text": "Thanks for that information.\n\nNow, could you tell me about your team? How big is it, and where are team members located? Are there any specific compliance, data residency, or air-gap constraints we should be aware of?"
    },
    {
      "role": "user",
      "text": "Our main development team is about 50 people, all located in our main office. We have strict data residency requirements, meaning all data must remain within our country's borders. We are not air-gapped."
    },
    {
      "role": "agent",
      "text": "I've opened the GitHub connection form for you to re-authenticate. Please complete the authentication process in the UI, and I'll await the result."
    },
    {
      "role": "user",
      "text": "Okay, I've opened it. Let me know when you need me to do something else."
    },
    {
      "role": "agent",
      "text": "I'm waiting for the result of the GitHub re-authentication. I'll let you know as soon as I have an update."
    },
    {
      "role": "user",
      "text": "Ok."
    },
    {
      "role": "agent",
      "text": "I'm checking the status of the GitHub re-authentication. I'll let you know the result shortly."
    },
    {
      "role": "user",
      "text": "Ok."
    }
